;;; `open` written as a fact's `:rule` clause loads, as a rule's name — M1f
;;; **W71**, register row `W71/fact-clause`, filed by S1f.5.23 (T1f.5.23.2,
;;; 2026-11-10).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `(p k :rule open)` says `p k` was derived by a rule named `open`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `open` is the verdict a rule's `:assert` states, `(open)` or `(open ?R)`,
;;; and is written nowhere else (the user's ruling on Q-M1f.66, 2026-11-10):
;;; here it is written as a fact's `:rule` clause, so the program is refused at
;;; the parse, at the `open`, and every command exits 1 (`ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `f62e34e1`, release: the program loads, root holds `(p k)`, and R is 2
;;; states, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at the parse since S1f.5.23 (T1f.5.23.3).

(relation a Thing :why "{?1} is an a")
(relation p Thing :why "{?1} is a p")
(relation q Thing :why "{?1} is a q")
(is-a k Thing)
(a k)
(p k :rule open)
